## Article

```catala
#[test] declaration scope A:
  context output a content integer
  context output b content boolean
  context output a_base content integer

#[test] declaration scope B:
  context output a content integer
  context output b content boolean
  scopeA scope A
  scopeAbis scope A

scope A:
  definition a_base equals 1
  definition a equals -1
  definition b equals a > 0

scope B:
  definition a equals 42
  definition b equals scopeA.b
  definition scopeA.a under condition a > 0 consequence equals scopeAbis.a_base
```



```catala-test-cli
$ catala Typecheck --check-invariants
┌─[WARNING]─
│
│  The sub-scope "scopeAbis" is not written in snake_case; consider renaming
│  it to "scope_abis".
│
├─➤ tests/scope/good/sub_scope.catala_en:13.3-12:
│    │
│ 13 │   scopeAbis scope A
│    │   ‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾
└─ Article
┌─[RESULT]─
│ All invariant checks passed
└─
┌─[RESULT]─
│ Typechecking successful!
└─
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope A
┌─[WARNING]─
│
│  The sub-scope "scopeAbis" is not written in snake_case; consider renaming
│  it to "scope_abis".
│
├─➤ tests/scope/good/sub_scope.catala_en:13.3-12:
│    │
│ 13 │   scopeAbis scope A
│    │   ‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾
└─ Article
┌─[RESULT]─ A ─
│ a = -1
│ b = false
│ a_base = 1
└─
```

```catala-test-cli
$ catala test-scope B
┌─[WARNING]─
│
│  The sub-scope "scopeAbis" is not written in snake_case; consider renaming
│  it to "scope_abis".
│
├─➤ tests/scope/good/sub_scope.catala_en:13.3-12:
│    │
│ 13 │   scopeAbis scope A
│    │   ‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾‾
└─ Article
┌─[RESULT]─ B ─
│ a = 42
│ b = true
└─
```
